# Agent Commands

When the user types any of the commands below, immediately read the corresponding skill file and follow its instructions. Do not ask for clarification — execute the workflow.

---

## `/mrreviewer <PR-number-or-URL>`

Accepts any of these formats:
- `/mrreviewer 42` — PR number (run inside the repo)
- `/mrreviewer https://github.com/owner/repo/pull/42` — full GitHub PR URL
- `/mrreviewer https://gitlab.com/org/repo/-/merge_requests/12` — full GitLab MR URL
- `/mrreviewer feature/my-branch` — branch name

Read and execute: `C:\Users\vamsi\.cursor\skills\review-mr\SKILL.md`

Extract the number and repo from whatever format the user provides. Pass both to Step 1.

---

## `/develop <ticket-id>`

**Example:** `/develop 123` or `/develop PROJ-456` or `/develop #78`

Read and execute: `C:\Users\vamsi\.cursor\skills\develop-from-ticket\SKILL.md`

Pass the provided ticket ID in Step 1 to determine ticket type and fetch requirements.

---

## `/build`

**Example:** `/build` or `/build feature-analytics-api`

Read and execute: `C:\Users\vamsi\.cursor\skills\build-feature-analytics-api\SKILL.md`

Start from Step 1 and build the full project in the current directory.

